# Karpathy engineering defaults (FitConnect)

Apply on every non-trivial change:

## 1. Think before coding
State the goal, constraints, and failure modes in one short block before edits. Prefer reading existing SoT over inventing parallel systems.

## 2. Simplicity first
Prefer the smallest change that preserves architecture rules (`AGENTS.md`, Strava-never-social, Health Connect core). Reject dependency bloat and second databases without necessity.

## 3. Surgical changes
One PR / one concern. Do not refactor outside the requested scope. Do not rewrite working offline/workout paths to rename enums unless product requires it.

## 4. Goal-driven execution
Define the acceptance evidence (test, AVD, API) before claiming done. Optional CI jobs are still quality signals — investigate failures; do not silently skip.

## Conflicts
Architecture + security rules win over this file. Tooling governance wins over “install everything.”
